DATA FOLDER - IND320
====================

This folder holds static raw data files, which the code reads but never
changes. The code also writes two local caches here (see the end),
which are not in git.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
reservoirs.csv
--------------------------------------------------------------------
What:     NVE Magasinstatistikk, weekly reservoir filling in Norway.
Source:   Provided with the course for Oblig1. Same data as NVE's
          Magasinstatistikk API:
          https://biapi.nve.no/magasinstatistikk/swagger/index.html
Period:   1995-01-08 to 2026-09-06, one row per area per week.
Columns:  dato_Id, omrType, omrnr, iso_aar, iso_uke, fyllingsgrad,
          kapasitet_TWh, fylling_TWh, neste_Publiseringsdato,
          fyllingsgrad_forrige_uke, endring_fyllingsgrad
Areas:    omrType = NO   -> all of Norway (omrnr 0)
          omrType = EL   -> electricity price areas NO1-NO5 (omrnr 1-5)
          omrType = VASS -> 3 water course areas (omrnr 1-3):
                            1 = East (Austlandet, Agder, parts of Rogaland)
                            2 = West (rest of Rogaland, most of Vestland)
                            3 = North (Møre og Romsdal, Trøndelag, Nord-Norge)
Used by:  Only Oblig1. The app and Oblig2 fetch the same data from the API.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
Budområder.zip
--------------------------------------------------------------------
What:     Shapefile with the electricity price areas (bidding zones)
          NO1-NO5. Matches omrType = EL in reservoirs.csv.
Source:   NVE Atlas, https://atlas.nve.no
          Layer: Nettanlegg > Nettområder > Budområder
Download: 09.11.2026

--------------------------------------------------------------------
NVE_Region.zip
--------------------------------------------------------------------
What:     Shapefile with NVE's five regions: RØ, RS, RV, RM, RN.
          Used as the precipitation areas that match omrType = VASS:
            East  = RS + RØ   (VASS 1)
            West  = RV        (VASS 2)
            North = RM + RN   (VASS 3)
          The regions are merged in code, not in the file.
Source:   NVE Atlas, https://atlas.nve.no
          Layer: Administrasjon > Administrative områder > NVE_Region
Download: 09.11.2026

--------------------------------------------------------------------
Norge_N5000.zip
--------------------------------------------------------------------
What:     Land cover map of Norway, scale 1:5 000 000 (coarse coastline),
          including the sea ("Havflate"). The sea is removed in code, and
          what is left is used to clip the areas to land before
          sampling locations.
Source:   NVE Atlas, https://atlas.nve.no (map data from Kartverket)
          Layer: Administrasjon > Administrative områder > Norge_N5000
Download: 09.11.2026

--------------------------------------------------------------------
Local caches (written by the code, not in git)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
weather_cells/
          Hourly ERA5 weather from Open-Meteo, one parquet file per
          grid cell and time interval:
          weather_cells/<settings code>/<start>-<end>/<lat>_<lon>.parquet
          The settings code is a short hash of the API settings, so data
          downloaded with other settings is never mixed in. Lets a stopped
          download continue where it left off. Written by
          src/ind320/openmeteo.py (the app and Oblig3). Can be deleted:
          it is downloaded again when needed.

entsoe_flows.parquet
          Local backup of the cross-border flows downloaded by Oblig2,
          so the notebook doesn't have to fetch them again (about 25
          minutes). Delete it to fetch fresh data.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
Notes
--------------------------------------------------------------------
- The zip files are read directly with geopandas, no need to unzip.
- The grid cells of each area (which ERA5 cells its random locations
  fall in, and how many) are computed from the three shapefiles by
  src/ind320/areas.py, with a fixed seed, so they are the same every
  time and don't need to be stored.
